---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title="Docs · MindContext — Constellation" description="Start using MindContext and understand its Markdown-first, Google Drive-backed knowledge model.">
  <div class="content-shell">
    <PageHero eyebrow="DOCUMENTATION" title="Start with files you can keep." description="MindContext is a browser-first Second Brain built around Markdown, user-owned storage and local projections." />

    <section class="docs-index">
      <a href="#getting-started"><span>01</span><strong>Getting started</strong><small>Connect Drive and create your first Second Brain.</small></a>
      <a href="#markdown"><span>02</span><strong>Markdown</strong><small>Portable syntax plus Obsidian-compatible conventions.</small></a>
      <a href="#workspace"><span>03</span><strong>Workspace</strong><small>Tabs, search, graph, properties and recovery.</small></a>
      <a href="#storage"><span>04</span><strong>Storage & privacy</strong><small>What stays in Drive and what stays local.</small></a>
    </section>

    <section class="prose-section" id="getting-started">
      <span class="eyebrow">01 · GETTING STARTED</span>
      <h2>Connect Google Drive</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open MindContext and authorize Google Drive.</li>
        <li>Create a new Second Brain or reopen one previously created by MindContext.</li>
        <li>Choose Blank or the optional PARA starter.</li>
        <li>Create Markdown notes and start linking ideas.</li>
      </ol>
      <p><a class="button primary" href={`${base}app/`}>Open the beta →</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose-section" id="markdown">
      <span class="eyebrow">02 · MARKDOWN</span>
      <h2>Markdown remains canonical</h2>
      <p>The editor supports standard Markdown authoring plus open/Obsidian-compatible conventions used by the knowledge projection.</p>
      <div class="syntax-grid">
        <code># Headings</code><code>[[Wikilinks]]</code><code>- [ ] Tasks</code><code>**Formatting**</code>
        <code>YAML properties</code><code>Callouts</code><code>$$ Math $$</code><code>Mermaid</code>
      </div>
      <p>Reading View also supports GFM tables, fenced-code highlighting, math and Mermaid. MindContext avoids adding hidden proprietary note structures.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose-section" id="workspace">
      <span class="eyebrow">03 · WORKSPACE</span>
      <h2>Derived context around your notes</h2>
      <p>Files, Search, Local Graph, Tags and Context panels are projections around the same Markdown files. Tabs and Edit/Read modes help with daily navigation without changing the underlying format.</p>
      <p>Pending edits are protected by browser-local recovery drafts before deferred Drive synchronization. Real conflicts can produce Markdown safety copies rather than silently overwriting content.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose-section" id="storage">
      <span class="eyebrow">04 · STORAGE & PRIVACY</span>
      <h2>Drive is canonical; local state is rebuildable</h2>
      <p>MindContext currently creates and rediscovers its own Drive workspace folders under the narrow <code>drive.file</code> permission. Arbitrary pre-existing Drive vault import is a future explicit workflow.</p>
      <p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}privacy/`}>Read the privacy model →</a></p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
